#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""calTUI — a read-only month calendar and paginated agenda for ICS subscriptions.

Q quit; C calendar; A agenda; T today; R refresh; S settings.
Calendar: left/right months, click a day for its agenda.
Agenda: up/down pages, never scrolls or opens event details.

Optional ~/.config/caltui/config.toml settings (existing URLs need no migration):
[agenda]
days_back = 30     # 1..366 days before the system local date
days_forward = 120 # 1..366 days after today, including that final day
[refresh]
minutes = 30      # 1..10080 minutes; shared by TUI, --next and --waybar
Values must be integers; booleans are rejected. Each missing key uses its default.
The one-year bounds limit local recurrence processing; feeds download in full.
The one-minute minimum avoids excessive requests; a week caps cache staleness.
The TUI marks and expands this window around today, regardless of navigation.
CLI next-event searches retain their independent horizon and --within filter.
S reloads settings; R forces downloads. No background service is required.

Dependencies: textual, icalendar, recurring-ical-events.
Uses Foot's 16 ANSI colors via Textual's ansi_color=True.
"""

